    "video": {
      "name": "Keto Recipe - Chocolate Roll Cake",
      "description": "Lately, I’ve been thinking about those little cake rolls that used to get backed in my school lunches. I wanted to recreate them…but elevate them in flavor and bring them over to the keto world. Instead of making a bunch of snack cakes, I decided to make one large roll that I could slice off and eat as I wanted (and eat, I did).\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\nChocolate Roll Cake\n1 cup almond flour\n4 tablespoons butter, melted\n3 large eggs\n¼ cup psyllium husk powder\n¼ cup cocoa powder\n¼ cup coconut milk\n¼ cup sour cream\n¼ cup erythritol\n1 teaspoon vanilla\n1 teaspoon baking powder\n\nCream Cheese Filling\n8 ounces cream cheese\n8 tablespoons butter\n¼ cup sour cream\n¼ cup erythritol\n¼ teaspoon liquid Stevia\n1 teaspoon vanilla\n\nNutrition Summary:\nThis makes 12 total slices. Each slice comes out to be 272.75 Calories, 26.07g Fats, 3.43g Net Carbs, and 5.44g Protein.\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 30 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
